diff --git a/docs/p6r-plugin-artifact-freshness.md b/docs/p6r-plugin-artifact-freshness.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..554f28646a9688ef4aa89bf65e0b7f2b74fb897a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/p6r-plugin-artifact-freshness.md
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# V2 plugin artifact freshness trial
+
+Set `BB_P6R_PLUGIN_ARTIFACT_FRESHNESS=1` in the server environment before a separately
+authorized start to enable this default-off trial. Unset it and restart to return
+to the existing freshness implementation; no source revert or deployment is
+required. This switch governs startup/reload behavior and cannot be a browser
+setting. This change does not authorize a restart.
+
+Mutable path/builtin v2 app bundles place their entry in
+`dist/.bb-artifacts/<generation>/app.js`. The old freshness probe checks only
+`dist/app.js` and treats its absence as stale, rebuilding an unchanged generation.
+Each rebuild chooses a random generation embedded in imports, invalidating the
+asset URLs and hashes even if logical source did not change.
+
+The trial validates the declared complete generation using the existing artifact
+loader (including safe paths, sizes and hashes), then compares source files and
+directories with the oldest declared artifact timestamp. It uses the same ignored
+paths as the development watcher. Newer source, deleted source (directory mtime),
+missing/corrupt artifacts and unreadable inputs remain stale. SDK compatibility
+still runs before this probe. V1, malformed metadata and a disabled switch call
+the unchanged legacy probe. Failed v2 validation never selects another generation.
+
+This adds one extra validation/hash pass on v2 artifact checks. It preserves the
+existing subsequent loader validation rather than weakening it. Tests cover
+stable URLs across repeated checks, source edits/deletion, corruption, missing
+chunks, generation mismatch and switch rollback. It does not change frontend
+loader concurrency, CSS ordering or the random-generation build format. Startup
+or cold-browser time saved requires a separately authorized production check.
diff --git a/packages/templates/src/templates/bb-guide-plugins.md b/packages/templates/src/templates/bb-guide-plugins.md
index 14ee833d177637d3c44deabb79f53be3b0b4a493..a5d86dd28e122627c625565b5d53d43851bd642d 100644
--- a/packages/templates/src/templates/bb-guide-plugins.md
+++ b/packages/templates/src/templates/bb-guide-plugins.md
@@ -343,3 +343,11 @@ plugins.
 `bb plugin update <id> --yes` starts a server job and waits by polling, so the activation stability check does not hold one HTTP request open. Add `--no-wait` to return immediately. Use `bb plugin update-jobs [job-id] --json` for progress and results, including automatic rollback. Queued/running updates continue after the CLI or app disconnects. Finished jobs remain for ten minutes; jobs do not survive server restarts. Running updates cannot be cancelled midway through activation.
 
 SDK: `plugins.applyUpdate({ pluginId })` waits; `plugins.experimental_startUpdate({ pluginId })` returns the job. Inspect with `plugins.experimental_updateJobs.list()` or `.get({ jobId })`. Raw HTTP callers opt in with `Prefer: respond-async`; legacy callers still receive the completed result.
+
+## V2 artifact freshness trial
+
+The downstream server flag `BB_P6R_PLUGIN_ARTIFACT_FRESHNESS=1` enables validation
+of the declared v2 generation before checking mutable plugin source timestamps.
+It avoids rebuilding unchanged v2 bundles solely because legacy `dist/app.js` is
+absent. It is off by default. Unset it and restart to roll back; no source revert
+is needed. Changing the server environment requires an authorized restart.
